      },
      "message": "fix(scripts): gate.sh test --exact never passes on zero tests\n\nReview findings on PR #133:\n- lib unit tests are named module::tests::fn, so --exact <fn> matched\n  nothing and passed green; lib names are now resolved from --list and\n  run --exact, integration tests keep --exact <fn>.\n- a filtered run that ran 0 tests is a FAIL (\"no test ran\").\n- the filter must be a fn name (it goes into a grep pattern).\n- the summary prints with printf '%b' (a % in a step name broke it).\n- README: quick tier includes the slow suites; pwsh runs gate.ps1's\n  finer quick tier on macOS/Linux.\n\nRefs #129\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
